import GroupApproximation.Analysis.CompressionTraceRigidity

/-!
# The compression route, run forwards: locally finite groups

`Analysis.CompressionTraceRigidity` proved that a group carrying an
asymptotically multiplicative compression family is locally finite.  This file
proves the converse, and thereby the first **unconditional** instance of the
conclusion of Tikuisis--White--Winter at an infinite-dimensional algebra in
this repository:

> for a countable locally finite group `G`, the canonical trace of `C⋆_r(G)`
> is a quasidiagonal trace ---
> `isQuasidiagonalTrace_canonicalReduced_of_locallyFinite`.

## Why local finiteness is exactly what the construction wants

The defect computation of the previous file said: a compression is exactly
multiplicative at `λ_g` when the window absorbs `g`.  Here that is upgraded
from one translation to everything.

* `inner_pointMass_leftRegular_apply` --- if `γ⁻¹ · e p` is again a compressed
  coordinate then the coefficient of `λ_γ v` at `δ_{e p}` is read off from the
  compressed coordinates alone.  This is the statement that no mass escapes,
  written for an arbitrary vector `v` rather than for a matrix entry.
* `compressionMap_mul_of_coe_eq_translationSum` --- hence a compression whose
  window is invariant under `γ₁, …, γ_m` is **exactly** multiplicative
  `φ(X b) = φ(X) φ(b)` for every `b`, whenever `X` is a linear combination of
  those translations.  Not asymptotically: exactly.
* `isAsymptoticallyMultiplicative_of_exhaustion` --- a family whose windows are
  subgroups exhausting `G` is therefore asymptotically multiplicative on all of
  `C⋆_r(G)`, by a three-term estimate against
  `ReducedGroupCStarTrace.exists_translationSum_approx`: exactly multiplicative
  on a dense set, contractive everywhere.

A countable locally finite group supplies such windows --- the subgroups
generated by longer and longer initial segments of an enumeration are finite
and exhaust the group --- and that is
`exists_compressionFamily_of_locallyFinite`.

## The characterization

Combining with the previous file:

```text
    the canonical trace of C⋆_r(G) has compression models
        ⟺  G is locally finite            (compressionFamily_iff_locallyFinite)
```

for countable `G`.  The elementary construction is therefore not merely
unproved beyond local finiteness --- it is **false** beyond it.  Since `ℤ` is
amenable and not locally finite, no compression family reaches the printed
sentence `INT.11`; what does is Tikuisis--White--Winter, and
`Analysis.TikuisisWhiteWinterUnconditional` records exactly that.

## Manuscript status

Supplies an unconditional route to `IsOperatorMF` for countable locally finite
groups (`isOperatorMF_of_locallyFinite_of_compression`), independent of the
LEF route of `Sofic.LocallyFiniteMF`.  Certifies no manuscript step that was
not already certified; its interest is that it is the boundary of the
elementary method.
-/

namespace GroupApproximation
namespace Quasidiagonal

open Filter ReducedGroupCStarTrace
open scoped InnerProductSpace Matrix.Norms.L2Operator

noncomputable section

universe u

variable {G : Type u} [Group G]

local instance locallyFiniteDecidableEq : DecidableEq G := Classical.decEq G

/-! ## Linear combinations of translations, inside the algebra -/

/-- The coercion of a finite combination of translations of the reduced
algebra is the same combination of translations of `ℓ²(G)`.  A bookkeeping
step: `Analysis.ReducedGroupCStarSpan` states density in the ambient algebra,
while the compression is defined on the subalgebra. -/
theorem coe_reducedTranslationSum {m : ℕ} (c : Fin m → ℂ) (γ : Fin m → G) :
    ((∑ i : Fin m, c i • reducedLeftRegular G (γ i) : ReducedGroupCStar G) :
        GroupHilbert G →L[ℂ] GroupHilbert G)
      = ∑ i : Fin m, c i • leftRegularOperator G (γ i) := by
  have h := map_sum ((reducedGroupCStarSubalgebra G).subtype)
    (fun i : Fin m ↦ c i • reducedLeftRegular G (γ i)) Finset.univ
  refine h.trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_)
  rfl

/-- **Density, inside the subalgebra.**  Every element of `C⋆_r(G)` is within
`ε` of a finite linear combination of translations, as an element of the
algebra rather than of the ambient operators. -/
theorem exists_reducedTranslationSum_approx (a : ReducedGroupCStar G) {ε : ℝ}
    (hε : 0 < ε) :
    ∃ (m : ℕ) (c : Fin m → ℂ) (γ : Fin m → G),
      ‖a - ∑ i : Fin m, c i • reducedLeftRegular G (γ i)‖ < ε := by
  obtain ⟨m, c, γ, h⟩ := exists_translationSum_approx G a.2 hε
  refine ⟨m, c, γ, ?_⟩
  have hnorm : ‖a - ∑ i : Fin m, c i • reducedLeftRegular G (γ i)‖
      = ‖(a : GroupHilbert G →L[ℂ] GroupHilbert G)
          - ((∑ i : Fin m, c i • reducedLeftRegular G (γ i) :
              ReducedGroupCStar G) : GroupHilbert G →L[ℂ] GroupHilbert G)‖ :=
    rfl
  rw [hnorm, coe_reducedTranslationSum c γ]
  exact h

/-! ## Exact multiplicativity on an invariant window -/

/-- **No mass escapes an invariant window.**

If `γ⁻¹ · e p` is again one of the compressed coordinates, then the
coefficient of `λ_γ v` at `δ_{e p}` is determined by the coefficients of `v`
at the compressed coordinates alone: the incidence matrix of the enumeration
already accounts for all of it.  This is the vector form of the vanishing
defect of `Analysis.CompressionTraceRigidity`, and it holds for an arbitrary
`v ∈ ℓ²(G)` --- in particular for `b δ_{e q}` with `b` anywhere in the
algebra, which is what exact multiplicativity needs. -/
theorem inner_pointMass_leftRegular_apply {k : ℕ} {e : Fin k → G}
    (he : Function.Injective e) {γ : G} {p : Fin k}
    (hγ : γ⁻¹ * e p ∈ Set.range e) (v : GroupHilbert G) :
    ⟪pointMass G (e p), leftRegularOperator G γ v⟫_ℂ
      = ∑ z : Fin k, incidence e γ p z * ⟪pointMass G (e z), v⟫_ℂ := by
  obtain ⟨z₀, hz₀⟩ := hγ
  have hep : e p = γ * e z₀ := by rw [hz₀, mul_inv_cancel_left]
  have hsum : (∑ z : Fin k, incidence e γ p z * ⟪pointMass G (e z), v⟫_ℂ)
      = ⟪pointMass G (e z₀), v⟫_ℂ := by
    rw [Finset.sum_eq_single z₀]
    · rw [incidence_eq_one hep, one_mul]
    · intro z _ hz
      have hne : ¬ (e p = γ * e z) := by
        intro hc
        refine hz (he ?_)
        rw [hz₀, hc, inv_mul_cancel_left]
      rw [incidence_eq_zero hne, zero_mul]
    · intro hcon
      exact absurd (Finset.mem_univ z₀) hcon
  rw [hsum, hz₀, ← ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_inner_left,
    ← ContinuousLinearMap.star_eq_adjoint,
    GroupVonNeumann.star_leftRegularOperator, leftRegular_pointMass]

/-- **A compression whose window absorbs the translations is exactly
multiplicative against them.**

`X` is any element of the algebra whose ambient form is the combination
`∑ cᵢ λ_{γᵢ}`, and every `γᵢ` preserves the window.  Then
`φ(X b) = φ(X) φ(b)` for *every* `b`, on the nose.  The proof is the incidence
computation of `inner_pointMass_leftRegular_apply` summed against the
coefficients, plus an exchange of the two finite sums. -/
theorem compressionMap_mul_of_coe_eq_translationSum {k : ℕ} {e : Fin k → G}
    (he : Function.Injective e) {m : ℕ} (c : Fin m → ℂ) (γ : Fin m → G)
    (hγ : ∀ i : Fin m, ∀ p : Fin k, (γ i)⁻¹ * e p ∈ Set.range e)
    (X b : ReducedGroupCStar G)
    (hX : (X : GroupHilbert G →L[ℂ] GroupHilbert G)
        = ∑ i : Fin m, c i • leftRegularOperator G (γ i)) :
    compressionMap e (X * b) = compressionMap e X * compressionMap e b := by
  funext p q
  have hXentry : ∀ z : Fin k, compressionMap e X p z
      = ∑ i : Fin m, c i * incidence e (γ i) p z := by
    intro z
    rw [compressionMap_apply, hX, _root_.sum_apply, inner_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_
    rw [_root_.smul_apply, inner_smul_right,
      inner_pointMass_leftRegular_pointMass]
  have hLHS : compressionMap e (X * b) p q
      = ∑ i : Fin m, ∑ z : Fin k, c i * (incidence e (γ i) p z
          * ⟪pointMass G (e z), (b : GroupHilbert G →L[ℂ] GroupHilbert G)
              (pointMass G (e q))⟫_ℂ) := by
    rw [compressionMap_apply]
    show ⟪pointMass G (e p), ((X : GroupHilbert G →L[ℂ] GroupHilbert G)
        * (b : GroupHilbert G →L[ℂ] GroupHilbert G))
          (pointMass G (e q))⟫_ℂ = _
    rw [mul_apply_eq_comp, hX, _root_.sum_apply, inner_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_
    rw [_root_.smul_apply, inner_smul_right,
      inner_pointMass_leftRegular_apply he (hγ i p), Finset.mul_sum]
  have hRHS : (compressionMap e X * compressionMap e b) p q
      = ∑ z : Fin k, ∑ i : Fin m, c i * (incidence e (γ i) p z
          * ⟪pointMass G (e z), (b : GroupHilbert G →L[ℂ] GroupHilbert G)
              (pointMass G (e q))⟫_ℂ) := by
    rw [Matrix.mul_apply]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun z _ ↦ ?_
    rw [hXentry z, compressionMap_apply, Finset.sum_mul]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_
    ring
  rw [hLHS, hRHS, Finset.sum_comm]

/-! ## Windows that exhaust the group -/

/-- **A compression family whose windows are subgroups exhausting `G` is
asymptotically multiplicative.**

The estimate is the standard three-term one, and both of its outer terms are
controlled by contractivity of the compression
(`norm_compressionMap_le`), which is where the completely positive structure
of the compression is used:

```text
  ‖φ(ab) − φ(a)φ(b)‖  ≤  ‖φ(ab) − φ(Xb)‖ + ‖φ(X)φ(b) − φ(a)φ(b)‖
                      ≤  2 ‖a − X‖ ‖b‖,
```

the middle term having vanished exactly, by
`compressionMap_mul_of_coe_eq_translationSum`, as soon as the window contains
the finitely many translations occurring in `X`. -/
theorem isAsymptoticallyMultiplicative_of_exhaustion
    (F : CompressionFamily G)
    (hsub : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ H : Subgroup G, Set.range (F.enum n) = (H : Set G))
    (hexh : ∀ g : G, ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ n : ℕ, N ≤ n → g ∈ Set.range (F.enum n)) :
    F.IsAsymptoticallyMultiplicative := by
  classical
  intro a b
  rw [Metric.tendsto_atTop]
  intro ε hε
  have hb1 : (0 : ℝ) < ‖b‖ + 1 := by positivity
  have hbne : (‖b‖ + 1) ≠ 0 := ne_of_gt hb1
  obtain ⟨m, c, γ, happ⟩ := exists_reducedTranslationSum_approx a
    (show (0 : ℝ) < ε / 2 / (‖b‖ + 1) by positivity)
  choose N hN using fun i : Fin m ↦ hexh (γ i)
  refine ⟨Finset.univ.sup N, fun n hn ↦ ?_⟩
  -- the window at stage `n` contains every translation occurring in `X`
  obtain ⟨H, hH⟩ := hsub n
  have hmemγ : ∀ i : Fin m, γ i ∈ H := by
    intro i
    have hle : N i ≤ n := le_trans (Finset.le_sup (Finset.mem_univ i)) hn
    have := hN i n hle
    rwa [hH] at this
  have hγ : ∀ i : Fin m, ∀ p : Fin (F.size n),
      (γ i)⁻¹ * F.enum n p ∈ Set.range (F.enum n) := by
    intro i p
    have hp : F.enum n p ∈ H := by
      have : F.enum n p ∈ Set.range (F.enum n) := ⟨p, rfl⟩
      rwa [hH] at this
    have : (γ i)⁻¹ * F.enum n p ∈ H := mul_mem (inv_mem (hmemγ i)) hp
    rwa [hH]
  -- the approximant, exactly multiplicated by the compression
  have hX : ((∑ i : Fin m, c i • reducedLeftRegular G (γ i) :
        ReducedGroupCStar G) : GroupHilbert G →L[ℂ] GroupHilbert G)
      = ∑ i : Fin m, c i • leftRegularOperator G (γ i) :=
    coe_reducedTranslationSum c γ
  have hmulX := compressionMap_mul_of_coe_eq_translationSum (F.injective n) c γ
    hγ (∑ i : Fin m, c i • reducedLeftRegular G (γ i)) b hX
  -- the three-term estimate
  have hcontr : ∀ y : ReducedGroupCStar G,
      ‖compressionMap (F.enum n) y‖ ≤ ‖y‖ :=
    fun y ↦ norm_compressionMap_le (F.injective n) y
  have htri : ∀ u v w : Matrix (naturalFiniteModel (F.size n))
      (naturalFiniteModel (F.size n)) ℂ, ‖u - w‖ ≤ ‖u - v‖ + ‖v - w‖ := by
    intro u v w
    rw [← dist_eq_norm, ← dist_eq_norm, ← dist_eq_norm]
    exact dist_triangle u v w
  have h1 : ‖compressionMap (F.enum n) (a * b)
      - compressionMap (F.enum n) (∑ i : Fin m, c i • reducedLeftRegular G (γ i))
        * compressionMap (F.enum n) b‖
      ≤ ‖a - ∑ i : Fin m, c i • reducedLeftRegular G (γ i)‖ * ‖b‖ := by
    rw [← hmulX, ← map_sub, ← sub_mul]
    exact le_trans (hcontr _) (norm_mul_le _ _)
  have h2 : ‖compressionMap (F.enum n)
        (∑ i : Fin m, c i • reducedLeftRegular G (γ i))
          * compressionMap (F.enum n) b
      - compressionMap (F.enum n) a * compressionMap (F.enum n) b‖
      ≤ ‖a - ∑ i : Fin m, c i • reducedLeftRegular G (γ i)‖ * ‖b‖ := by
    rw [← sub_mul, ← map_sub]
    refine le_trans (Matrix.l2_opNorm_mul _ _) ?_
    have hXa : ‖compressionMap (F.enum n)
        ((∑ i : Fin m, c i • reducedLeftRegular G (γ i)) - a)‖
        ≤ ‖a - ∑ i : Fin m, c i • reducedLeftRegular G (γ i)‖ :=
      le_trans (hcontr _) (le_of_eq (norm_sub_rev _ _))
    exact mul_le_mul hXa (hcontr b) (norm_nonneg _) (norm_nonneg _)
  have hsplit := htri (compressionMap (F.enum n) (a * b))
    (compressionMap (F.enum n) (∑ i : Fin m, c i • reducedLeftRegular G (γ i))
      * compressionMap (F.enum n) b)
    (compressionMap (F.enum n) a * compressionMap (F.enum n) b)
  -- and the arithmetic
  have hmul_lt : ‖a - ∑ i : Fin m, c i • reducedLeftRegular G (γ i)‖ * ‖b‖
      < ε / 2 := by
    have hstrict := mul_lt_mul_of_pos_right happ hb1
    have hle : ‖a - ∑ i : Fin m, c i • reducedLeftRegular G (γ i)‖ * ‖b‖
        ≤ ‖a - ∑ i : Fin m, c i • reducedLeftRegular G (γ i)‖ * (‖b‖ + 1) := by
      refine mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ?_ (norm_nonneg _)
      linarith
    have heq : ε / 2 / (‖b‖ + 1) * (‖b‖ + 1) = ε / 2 := by
      field_simp
    linarith
  have hdist : dist (‖F.map n (a * b) - F.map n a * F.map n b‖) (0 : ℝ)
      = ‖compressionMap (F.enum n) (a * b)
        - compressionMap (F.enum n) a * compressionMap (F.enum n) b‖ := by
    rw [Real.dist_eq, sub_zero]
    exact abs_of_nonneg (norm_nonneg _)
  rw [hdist]
  linarith

/-! ## Countable locally finite groups supply such a family -/

/-- **A countable locally finite group has an exhausting compression family.**

Enumerate `G` as `f 0, f 1, …`; the subgroup generated by `f 0, …, f n` is
finite by local finiteness, and these subgroups exhaust `G`.  Compressing to
each of them in turn is the family. -/
theorem exists_compressionFamily_of_locallyFinite (G : Type u) [Group G]
    [Countable G] (hG : IsLocallyFiniteGroup G) :
    ∃ F : CompressionFamily G,
      (∀ n : ℕ, 0 < F.size n) ∧ F.IsAsymptoticallyMultiplicative := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨f, hf⟩ := exists_surjective_nat G
  have hdata : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ (k : ℕ) (e : Fin k → G), 0 < k ∧ Function.Injective e
      ∧ (∃ H : Subgroup G, Set.range e = (H : Set G))
      ∧ ∀ j : ℕ, j ≤ n → f j ∈ Set.range e := by
    intro n
    obtain ⟨H, hHfin, hHmem⟩ := hG ((Finset.range (n + 1)).image f)
    haveI : Finite H := hHfin
    letI : Fintype H := Fintype.ofFinite H
    have hrange : Set.range (fun i : Fin (Fintype.card H) ↦
        (((Fintype.equivFin H).symm i : H) : G)) = (H : Set G) := by
      ext x
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨i, rfl⟩
        exact ((Fintype.equivFin H).symm i).2
      · intro hx
        exact ⟨Fintype.equivFin H ⟨x, hx⟩, by simp⟩
    refine ⟨Fintype.card H, fun i ↦ (((Fintype.equivFin H).symm i : H) : G),
      Fintype.card_pos_iff.mpr ⟨1⟩, ?_, ⟨H, hrange⟩, ?_⟩
    · intro i j hij
      exact (Fintype.equivFin H).symm.injective (Subtype.ext hij)
    · intro j hj
      have hmem : f j ∈ H :=
        hHmem (f j) (Finset.mem_image.mpr ⟨j, Finset.mem_range.mpr
          (by omega), rfl⟩)
      rw [hrange]
      exact hmem
  choose K E hKpos hEinj hEsub hEmem using hdata
  refine ⟨⟨K, E, hEinj⟩, hKpos, ?_⟩
  refine isAsymptoticallyMultiplicative_of_exhaustion ⟨K, E, hEinj⟩
    (fun n ↦ hEsub n) ?_
  intro g
  obtain ⟨j, rfl⟩ := hf g
  exact ⟨j, fun n hn ↦ hEmem n j hn⟩

/-! ## The unconditional instance of the conclusion of TWW -/

/-- **The canonical trace of a countable locally finite group is
quasidiagonal.**

An inhabitant of `Quasidiagonal.QuasidiagonalTraceModel` at an
infinite-dimensional algebra, with no input at all: the first in this
repository.  It is the conclusion of Tikuisis--White--Winter for these groups,
proved rather than assumed. -/
theorem isQuasidiagonalTrace_canonicalReduced_of_locallyFinite (G : Type u)
    [Group G] [Countable G] (hG : IsLocallyFiniteGroup G) :
    IsQuasidiagonalTrace (canonicalReducedTrace G) := by
  obtain ⟨F, hpos, hmul⟩ := exists_compressionFamily_of_locallyFinite G hG
  exact F.isQuasidiagonalTrace hpos hmul

/-- **Countable locally finite groups are operator-MF, by quasidiagonality.**

The printed route of `INT.11` --- *quasidiagonality of the canonical trace,
then the corona argument* --- run end to end with no citation, on the class
where the construction works.  `Sofic.LocallyFiniteMF.isOperatorMF_of_locallyFinite`
reaches the same conclusion through exact finite models and LEF; this is the
same conclusion through the trace, and the two share no step. -/
theorem isOperatorMF_of_locallyFinite_of_compression (G : Type u) [Group G]
    [Countable G] (hG : IsLocallyFiniteGroup G) : IsOperatorMF G :=
  QuasidiagonalMF.isOperatorMF_of_isQuasidiagonalCanonicalTrace ucpContractive G
    (isQuasidiagonalTrace_canonicalReduced_of_locallyFinite G hG)

/-! ## The characterization -/

/-- **The compression route certifies exactly the locally finite groups.**

Forwards, `Analysis.CompressionTraceRigidity`: an asymptotically
multiplicative family forces every finite subset into a finite subgroup.
Backwards, this file: a countable locally finite group has such a family.

So the elementary construction is not merely unproved outside local
finiteness --- it is refuted there.  Every countable amenable group that is
not locally finite, `ℤ` first among them, is a group for which
Tikuisis--White--Winter asserts a conclusion that no compression family can
witness. -/
theorem compressionFamily_iff_locallyFinite (G : Type u) [Group G]
    [Countable G] :
    (∃ F : CompressionFamily G,
        (∀ n : ℕ, 0 < F.size n) ∧ F.IsAsymptoticallyMultiplicative)
      ↔ IsLocallyFiniteGroup G := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨F, hpos, hmul⟩
    exact isLocallyFiniteGroup_of_isAsymptoticallyMultiplicative F
      (Filter.Eventually.of_forall hpos) hmul
  · exact exists_compressionFamily_of_locallyFinite G

end

end Quasidiagonal
end GroupApproximation
